# Generated from palettes.toml by `theme` — do not edit; edit the .tmpl.
# xsettingsd config. Rendered by ~/.local/bin/theme.
#
# xsettingsd serves XSettings to XWayland clients (PLAYBOOK.md §2.2) — native
# Wayland clients get their settings from gsettings instead (see
# sway/.config/sway/scripts/import-gsettings).
#
# NOTE: xsettingsd is NOT INSTALLED on this machine — not merely stopped. There
# is no binary, nothing starts one, and nothing reads this file: as rendered it
# is inert. "Not currently running" understated that for a long time and read
# as if a daemon were one `systemctl start` away.
#
# It is tracked and kept correct anyway, because it costs one template and the
# alternative is discovering at install time that the one GTK mechanism reaching
# XWayland clients was never themed. `pacman -S xsettingsd` and something to
# start it are what turn this file live; until then, XWayland clients fall back
# to whatever gtk-3.0/settings.ini and Xft give them.
Net/ThemeName "{{gtk_theme_name}}"
Net/IconThemeName "Papirus-Dark"
Gtk/CursorThemeName "Qogir-Dark"
Net/EnableEventSounds 1
Net/EnableInputFeedbackSounds 0
Xft/Antialias 1
Xft/Hinting 1
Xft/HintStyle "hintslight"
Xft/RGBA "rgb"
